WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
Missing audit logs leave teams unable to reconstruct important events.

2
00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:17.201
Applications should capture authentication activity, authorization failures, administrative actions, sensitive data access, configuration changes, and high-risk workflow events.

3
00:00:17.201 --> 00:00:21.731
Poor alerting creates noise without action or misses the events that matter most.

4
00:00:21.731 --> 00:00:28.856
Alerts should focus on anomalies, suspicious access, high-risk changes, and activity affecting sensitive data.

5
00:00:28.856 --> 00:00:33.206
Delayed incident detection increases attacker dwell time and impact.

6
00:00:33.206 --> 00:00:40.141
Without monitoring and review, compromise, insider abuse, and data access anomalies may continue unnoticed.

7
00:00:40.141 --> 00:00:43.793
Incomplete monitoring can also weaken SOC 2 readiness.

8
00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:51.595
Logs need retention, integrity, ownership, review procedures, and escalation paths that support investigation and evidence.

9
00:00:51.595 --> 00:00:57.871
Centralize logging from applications, identity systems, infrastructure, and cloud services.

10
00:00:57.871 --> 00:01:01.314
Integrate telemetry with SIEM or monitoring workflows.

11
00:01:01.314 --> 00:01:05.305
Create security alerting and review processes for high-risk events.

12
00:01:05.305 --> 00:01:09.236
Selected SOC 2 mappings for this topic include CC7.

13
00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:11.830
2 - Monitoring activities; CC7.

14
00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:14.455
3 - Incident detection and response support.
